<title>FINLAND: AKTIA BANK SEES 4.0 PCT FINNISH 1997 GDP GROWTH.</title>
<headline>AKTIA BANK SEES 4.0 PCT FINNISH 1997 GDP GROWTH.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Aktia Bank said in a forecast</p>
<p>on Tuesday it expected Finland's gross domestic product (GDP) to</p>
<p>grow by 4.0 percent this year and by 3.5 percent in 1998.</p>
<p>&quot;The Finnish economy continues on a strong growth path,&quot;</p>
<p>Aktia said in a statement. &quot;The outlook for the Finnish economy</p>
<p>is excellent at the moment,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>Inflation would remain slow, Aktia said, forecasting a 1.0</p>
<p>percent annual average rise in consumer prices this year, and a</p>
<p>rise of 2.0 percent in 1998.</p>
<p>Key figures in Aktia's April 29, 1997 forecast:</p>
<p>			   1997	 1998	  1996</p>
<p> GDP		     +4.0	 +3.5	  +3.2</p>
<p> Exports		 +7.0	 +5.0	  +3.8</p>
<p> Imports		 +6.0	 +7.0	  +4.9</p>
<p> Private consumption +4.0	 +4.0	  +3.5</p>
<p> Private investment  +5.0	 +7.0	  +6.4</p>
<p> Public investment   +/-0	 +/-0	  +0.1</p>
<p> CPI		     +1.0	 +2.0	  +0.6</p>
<p> Unemployment	  15.5	 14.6	  16.3</p>
<p> C/A (FIM billion)    +18	  +15	 +19.2</p>
<p>--Helsinki newsroom +358-9-680 50 245, e-mail news@reuters.fi</p>
